259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 705 0 R
/E (In this Arduino program, a tilt sensor is connected to pin 2 \(TILT_PIN\), a buzzer to pin 7 \(BUZZER_PIN\), and an LED to pin 6 \(LED_PIN\).)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 706 0 R
/E (The setup\(\) function runs once when the Arduino starts. It sets the tilt sensor as INPUT and both the buzzer and LED as OUTPUT using pinMode\(\). Initially, both the buzzer and LED are turned OFF using digitalWrite\(\).)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 707 0 R
/E (The loop\(\) function runs continuously. It reads the tilt sensor value using digitalRead\(\) and stores it in tiltState.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 708 0 R
/E (If tilt is detected \(HIGH\), both the buzzer and LED turn ON. If there is no tilt \(LOW\), both turn OFF.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
263 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (So overall, the Arduino activates the buzzer and LED when tilt is detected and turns them OFF otherwise.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
