<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 735 0 R
/E (In this Arduino program, a tilt sensor is connected to pin 2 \(TILT_PIN\), and two LEDs are connected to pins 6 and 5 \(LED1_PIN and LED2_PIN\).)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 736 0 R
/E (The setup\(\) function runs once when the Arduino starts. It sets the tilt sensor as INPUT and both LEDs as OUTPUT using pinMode\(\). Initially, both LEDs are turned OFF.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 737 0 R
/E (The loop\(\) function runs continuously. It reads the tilt sensor value using digitalRead\(\) and stores it in tiltState.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
361 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 738 0 R
/E (If tilt is detected \(HIGH\), both LEDs turn ON. If there is no tilt \(LOW\), both LEDs turn OFF.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
362 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
